# Project layout

Shroud is an end-to-end encrypted chat app: **Rust + PostgreSQL server** and a **native iOS app (Swift/SwiftUI)**.

| Path | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `iOS-App.pen` | Design source of truth (Pencil file — MCP tools only). |
| `emoji/` | Apple emoji PNG assets referenced by the design file. Do not delete or rename. |
| `server/` | Rust workspace (Axum API, message relay, push, migrations under `server/migrations/postgres/`). |
| `ios/` | Native iOS app (Swift/SwiftUI, Xcode project). |
| `docs/` | Architecture decisions, protocol notes, API contracts. |

## Rules

- Create `server/` and `ios/` following this layout when backend/app code is first added; do not invent parallel top-level folders (`backend/`, `app/`, `mobile/`).
- Shared protocol definitions (message envelope, API DTOs) live in `server/` and are mirrored in Swift by hand — when one side changes, update the other in the same change set (`regression-testing.mdc`).
- Screens in the iOS app must map 1:1 to screens in `iOS-App.pen`; new screens are designed in the `.pen` file first, then implemented.
